`max_window_sum(xs, k)` returns the largest sum of any `k` consecutive elements of `xs`, or None when `k` is not between 1 and `len(xs)`.

The implementation below has a bug: it fails at least one of the tests shown. Fix it so every test passes. The fixed function is also run against held-out tests of the same behavior, so fix the bug itself rather than special-casing these tests.

```python
def max_window_sum(xs, k):
    if k <= 1 or k > len(xs):
        return None
    total = sum(xs[:k])
    best = total
    for i in range(k, len(xs)):
        total += xs[i] - xs[i - k]
        if total > best:
            best = total
    return best
```

